Reconstructed catches and stock assessments

Reconstructed catches from Sea Around Us
We compile the reconstructed catch datasets from the Sea Around Us project. These data correspond to the Sea Around Us spatialized catches contained within three polygons: FAO area 34, the Canary Current LME (LME 27), and the Guinea Current LME (LME 28).
Since the LMEs are almost entirely inscribed in the FAO area, we deduct the LME catches from those of the FAO area. This gives the catches on the high seas, as opposed to the catches in the LMEs, which cover most of the EEZs and the entire continental shelf of the region.
Since the LMEs are not entirely inscribed in the FAO zone (in particular LME 28), negative values are generated when computing the high seas catches. In those cases the high seas catch is set to 0 t for the taxon.

# Helper function (the csv downloaded from the website contained missing ',' when the last column in NA)

fix_csv_trailing_missing_field &lt;- function(input_csv, output_csv, expected_cols = 15) {
  lines &lt;- read_lines(input_csv)

  # Store header and data separately
  header &lt;- lines[1]
  data_lines &lt;- lines[-1]

  # Define expected number of columns from header
  expected_cols &lt;- str_count(header, ",") + 1

  fixed_data_lines &lt;- vapply(data_lines, function(line) {
    # Split on commas outside quotes
    fields &lt;- strsplit(line, ",(?=(?:[^\"]*\"[^\"]*\")*[^\"]*$)", perl = TRUE)[[1]]

    if (length(fields) == expected_cols - 1) {
      # Insert empty field as last column (landed_value missing)
      fields &lt;- c(fields, "")
    }

    paste(fields, collapse = ",")
  }, FUN.VALUE = character(1))

  # Write back with original header
  write_lines(c(header, fixed_data_lines), output_csv)

  message("CSV fixed and saved to: ", output_csv)

  invisible(TRUE)
}

